  "metadata": {
    "title": "Raydium Tops $1 Trillion in Volume as RAY Token Lists on Robinhood and Revolut",
    "byline": null,
    "published_at": null,
    "site_name": "finance.yahoo.com",
    "language": null
  },
  "content": {
    "text": "Raydium's RAY (CRYPTO: $RAY) token has landed on Robinhood (NASDAQ: $HOOD) and Revolut after the Solana (CRYPTO: $SOL) based decentralized exchange crossed $1 trillion in cumulative trading volume, giving one of Solana's largest DeFi assets a wider path into mainstream retail finance.\nThe back-to-back listings put RAY inside two regulated consumer platforms spanning the United States, the United Kingdom and the European Union. Robinhood reports roughly 25 million funded accounts, while Revolut has more than 50 million users globally. Raydium said RAY is the first token from a Solana-based decentralized exchange to be available on both apps.\nThe listing milestone follows a year of stronger on-chain activity for Raydium, which has become the highest-volume decentralized exchange on Solana across recent measurement periods. The protocol said it has now processed more than $1 trillion in on-chain trading volume and generated $370 million in lifetime protocol revenue.\nMore From Cryptoprowl:\n-\nEightco Secures $125 Million Investment From Bitmine And ARK Invest, Shares Surge\n-\nStanley Druckenmiller Says Stablecoins Could Reshape Global Finance\nRaydium is also trying to position that liquidity beyond standard token trading. Tokenized equity volume on the protocol crossed $1 billion this month, with U.S.-listed stocks including Tesla (NASDAQ: $TSLA) and Nvidia (NASDAQ: $NVDA) routing through Raydium liquidity pools through xStocks and related issuer partnerships. The protocol also supports tokenized real-world asset activity tied to Figure's PRIME consortium and stablecoin pools including Circle's USDC (CRYPTO: $USDC) and PayPal USD (CRYPTO: $PYUSD).\nChief marketing officer Ben Ungvari said \"there is currently no other DeFi token on both Robinhood and Revolut,\" adding that the listings followed the protocol's scale across Solana liquidity pools.\nThat distribution gives Raydium a new layer of visibility at a time when DeFi venues are trying to move from crypto-native usage toward consumer finance access. It also gives Solana's on-chain market structure a more direct connection to retail apps that already serve stock, commodity and digital asset traders.\nRaydium still depends on users choosing on-chain liquidity over centralized venues, but the latest listings make that access less distant for mainstream traders.\nRaydium (CRYPTO: RAY) is currently trading at $0.70 U.S. per digital token.",
